## Randomness

All randomness is seeded explicitly, so results do not depend on how many cores are used (tested). A master seed in `params.yaml` (`master_seed`) generates a seed for every stream:


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
derive_seed
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

```
function (master_seed, rep, scenario_index, type_index = 0L) 
{
    as.integer((master_seed + 1009 * rep + 100003 * scenario_index + 
        7919 * type_index)%%.Machine$integer.max)
}
```


:::
:::


Seeds depend on the replication number, the scenario index and the event-type index, so the same replication in different scenarios shares nothing accidentally, and the baseline and control arms of the control study share seeds on purpose (paired comparison). Bootstrap and frequency-severity simulations take a seed derived the same way.

## Parameters

Every simulator parameter lives in one file. `status: assumption` marks values that are plausible choices, not calibrated estimates.


```{.r .cell-code}
cat("```yaml\n", paste(readLines("params.yaml"), collapse = "\n"), "\n```\n", sep = "")
```

```yaml
# Single source of truth for all simulator parameters.
# status: "assumption" = chosen for plausibility, not calibrated to data.
# Every value is synthetic; replace with client data in a real engagement.
master_seed: 20261009

firm:
  aum_usd: 5.0e+9        # stylised mid-size buy-side firm; used only to express losses in bps of AUM
  status: assumption

horizon:
  n_origin: 40          # origin quarters (10 years); evaluation date = end of quarter 40
  n_lag: 40             # discovery lags 0..39 inside the window; lag >= 40 is "tail"
  status: assumption

exposure:
  base: 1.0
  growth_per_quarter: 0.01   # ~4% p.a. volume growth; range 0 - 0.03
  status: assumption

replication:
  n_reps: 200
  n_boot: 1000          # BootChainLadder resamples per triangle
  runs:                 # scenario -> granularities scored (annual = 4 quarters per period)
    baseline: [annual, quarterly]
    heavy_tail_shock: [annual]
    control_improvement: [annual]
    exposure_growth: [annual]
  recent_quarters: 4    # "recent" = latest 4 origin quarters (1 annual period)
  status: assumption

mlreserve:              # experimental comparator, see mlreserve.qmd
  n_reps: 30
  commit: 30cc7a8402f29713d3f53861e42b092cbc6946f1   # thierrymoudiki/ChainLadder (fork of mages/ChainLadder)
  configs:              # blog setting first; the rest are variants incl. the package default (factor features), all scored on the same replications
    rf_asinh_numeric: {learner: ranger, features: numeric, transform: asinh}
    rf_raw_numeric: {learner: ranger, features: numeric, transform: none}
    rf_raw_both: {learner: ranger, features: both, transform: none}
    rf_raw_factor: {learner: ranger, features: factor, transform: none}      # package default features
    svm_raw_numeric: {learner: svm, features: numeric, transform: none}
    svm_raw_factor: {learner: svm, features: factor, transform: none}
  status: assumption

controls:               # detection controls; effects are applied as shifts to the lag distribution
  recon_automation:
    description: Automated daily position/cash reconciliation against prime-broker statements
    annual_cost_usd: 400000          # assumption; range 250k - 600k
    lag_shift:
      nav_error: {slow_meanlog: -0.4, w_fast: 0.10}
      unauthorized_trading: {slow_meanlog: -0.4}
    status: assumption
  independent_pnl_verification:
    description: Independent P&L and limit-breach verification with prime-broker position feed
    annual_cost_usd: 700000          # assumption; range 400k - 1.2M
    lag_shift:
      trade_error: {w_fast: 0.05}
      nav_error: {slow_meanlog: -0.3}
      unauthorized_trading: {slow_meanlog: -0.8, w_fast: 0.15}
    status: assumption

event_types:
  trade_error:                       # Basel: Execution, Delivery & Process Mgmt
    lambda: 60                       # events / quarter at exposure 1; range 30 - 120
    lag: {w_fast: 0.85, p_fast: 0.80, slow_meanlog: 0.5, slow_sdlog: 0.8}
    severity: {meanlog: 7.8, sdlog: 1.2, p_tail: 0.03, tail_q: 0.95, xi: 0.2, beta: 8000, lag_elasticity: 0.02}
    status: assumption
  nav_error:                         # Basel: EDPM / Clients, Products & Business Practices
    lambda: 6                        # range 3 - 15
    lag: {w_fast: 0.50, p_fast: 0.40, slow_meanlog: 1.5, slow_sdlog: 0.8}
    severity: {meanlog: 10.3, sdlog: 1.4, p_tail: 0.05, tail_q: 0.95, xi: 0.3, beta: 80000, lag_elasticity: 0.05}
    status: assumption
  unauthorized_trading:              # Basel: Internal Fraud (incl. limit and mandate breaches)
    lambda: 0.3                      # ~1.2 per year; range 0.1 - 0.8
    lag: {w_fast: 0.10, p_fast: 0.30, slow_meanlog: 2.0, slow_sdlog: 0.9}
    severity: {meanlog: 12.4, sdlog: 1.6, p_tail: 0.08, tail_q: 0.90, xi: 0.6, beta: 1500000, lag_elasticity: 0.08}
    status: assumption

scenarios:
  baseline: {}
  heavy_tail_shock:
    injected_events:                 # absolute-dollar events added to the baseline
      - {type: unauthorized_trading, origin: 12, lag: 15, severity: 60000000}
      - {type: unauthorized_trading, origin: 20, lag: 22, severity: 40000000}
  control_improvement:
    control_shift: {calendar_quarter: 24, reduction: 0.5}   # remaining time-to-discovery halves after Q24
  exposure_growth:
    exposure: {growth_per_quarter: 0.03}
```


